<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/3/eng@/~part_VII__cl_41__subsec_2> <https://schema.org/text> "Where the person to whom there has been addressed a registered letter containing any notice which may be given under this Act or any subsidiary legislation made thereunder is informed orally or in writing of the fact that there is a registered letter awaiting him at a post office, and such person refuses, neglects or fails to take delivery of such registered letter, such notice shall be deemed to have been served upon him on the date on which he is so informed. Power of Board to make rules"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/3/eng@> .
